    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong></p><p>ALT 1 Use of pV = nRT to get T<sub>B</sub> = 1200 «K» AND <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P_{C}=\"></span>«<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{{P}_{A} {{V}_{A}}^{\\frac{5}{3}}}{{{V}_{C}}^{\\frac{5}{3}}} = \\frac{( 2 \\times  {10}^{6} ) {( 1 \\times  {10}^{- 3} )}^{\\frac{5}{3}}}{{( 1 \\times  {10}^{- 2} )}^{\\frac{5}{3}}} =\"></span>»<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"43 089\"></span>«<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Pa\"></span>» ✓ T<sub>C</sub> = 4.3×10<sup>4</sup>×1200/2.0×10<sup>5</sup> OR T<sub>C</sub> = 258 «K» ✓ ALT 2 <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P_{C}=\"></span>«<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{{P}_{A} {{V}_{A}}^{\\frac{5}{3}}}{{{V}_{C}}^{\\frac{5}{3}}} = \\frac{( 2 \\times  {10}^{6} ) {( 1 \\times  {10}^{- 3} )}^{\\frac{2}{3}}}{{( 1 \\times  {10}^{- 2} )}^{\\frac{2}{3}}} =\"></span>»<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"43 089\"></span>«<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Pa\"></span>» ✓ Use of p<sub>C</sub>V<sub>C</sub> = nRT<sub>C</sub> = (43 089)(1×10<sup>−2</sup>) = (0.2)(8.31) T<sub>C</sub> OR T<sub>C</sub> = 259 «K» ✓   Must see full substitution OR answer to 3 (or more) significant figures.</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong></p><p>Use of ΔU = −3/2 n R ΔT ✔ W = «(3/2)(0.2)(8.31)(1200−259) » = «−»2350 «J» ✔</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong></p><p>work done by the gas in the isothermal process is larger ✓ net work is done by the gas ✓ net/total work is positive ✓ work done by the gas is greater than work done on the gas ✓</p></section>"
