  "question": {
    "html": "<section class=\"context\"><p>The pressure–volume diagram shows a 3-stage cyclic process of 0.20 moles of an ideal gas in a closed container. A–B is an isothermal process. C–A is an adiabatic process.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The following data are available:</p>\n<table><tbody><tr><td></td><td><p>Pressure at A</p></td><td><p>= 2.0 × 10<sup>6</sup> Pa</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>Volume at A</p></td><td><p>= 1.0 × 10<sup>−3</sup> m<sup>3</sup></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>Pressure at B</p></td><td><p>= 2.0 × 10<sup>5</sup> Pa</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>Volume at B</p></td><td><p>= 1.0 × 10<sup>−2</sup> m<sup>3</sup></p></td></tr></tbody></table></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> Show that the temperature at C is about 260 K. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> Determine the work done by the gas in C–A. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong> Outline why this cycle can be used for a heat engine. [1]</p></section>"
  },
